※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4366

※ **`⎕address` of a function is where the code of one of the system's
※ convention is**, which is all such a value is.  A function of the language's
※ own convention expects what it brought in first, so its code alone is
※ nothing anything else could call.

let std := ⎕import("std")

fn tripled(x: u64) → u64:
    x × 3u64

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let f: fn(u64) → u64 = tripled
    if ⎕address(f) ≠ 0u64: 0u6 else: 1u6
